WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.232
Accessibility should shape media production from the beginning.

00:00:03.232 --> 00:00:06.756
Readable contrast, plain language, alt text planning, captions, transcripts,

00:00:06.756 --> 00:00:12.629
and keyboard and screen-reader considerations all affect whether learners can access and understand the course.

00:00:12.629 --> 00:00:16.545
Accessibility also improves the experience for learners on small screens,

00:00:16.545 --> 00:00:19.286
in noisy environments, or under time constraints.

00:00:19.286 --> 00:00:23.201
Alt text should describe the instructional purpose of meaningful images.

00:00:23.201 --> 00:00:27.508
Decorative images may not need detailed descriptions, but diagrams, screenshots, charts,

00:00:27.508 --> 00:00:29.466
and process visuals usually do.

00:00:29.466 --> 00:00:33.381
Captions and transcripts should be available for audio and video.

00:00:33.381 --> 00:00:38.863
Plain language helps learners focus on the concept rather than decoding unnecessarily complex writing.

00:00:38.863 --> 00:00:41.995
File size and performance are production concerns too.

00:00:41.995 --> 00:00:43.561
Oversized images, heavy videos,

00:00:43.561 --> 00:00:47.477
and unnecessary effects can slow course loading or frustrate learners.

00:00:47.477 --> 00:00:50.218
Export settings should balance quality with performance.

00:00:50.218 --> 00:00:55.308
A beautiful asset that makes a module sluggish may harm the learning experience,

00:00:55.308 --> 00:00:58.049
especially for remote learners or constrained networks.

00:00:58.049 --> 00:01:01.573
Stakeholder review should confirm accuracy, tone, completeness, brand fit,

00:01:01.573 --> 00:01:02.747
and learner relevance.

00:01:02.747 --> 00:01:06.663
Media QA should check readability, audio quality, captions, transcripts, links,

00:01:06.663 --> 00:01:09.403
visual consistency, file naming, and export quality.

00:01:09.403 --> 00:01:12.927
LMS packaging considerations should include launch behavior, tracking requirements,

00:01:12.927 --> 00:01:16.451
and whether media loads correctly from the published package.

00:01:16.451 --> 00:01:19.584
Quality assurance is not a single final click-through.

00:01:19.584 --> 00:01:21.541
It is a production habit.

00:01:21.541 --> 00:01:23.107
Review scripts before recording.

00:01:23.107 --> 00:01:24.674
Check visuals before export.

00:01:24.674 --> 00:01:26.240
Confirm captions with audio.

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:27.414
Verify downloadable resources.

00:01:27.414 --> 00:01:30.547
Test the course package in the intended environment.

00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:36.420
The goal is to ensure assets support learning for more people across devices and contexts.
